  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving vision for communities in Zimbabwe&apos;s Midland Province, by strengthening eye health services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be implemented in the Midlands Province, which is 350 km long, making its population (current estimate: 1,910,505) significantly dispersed and hard to reach. All of the province&#x201a;&#xc4;&#xf4;s eight districts will be covered, namely Chirumanzu, Gokwe North, Gokwe South, Gweru, Kwekwe, Mberengwa, Shurugwi and Zvishavane</narrative>
  </description>
